From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:31:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 113/148] hjviewer: support links, the waiting room and the
 staff mark's screens (TV-W6 controller)

TV-W6 S2, S9, S10: from a 1.9 hjv-api, whose support-code answer also
carries a sound `link` and `wait`, the core hands S2 the whole link and a
slot and keeps the waiting number in memory only. S2 then offers [Close]
[Copy code] [Copy link] [Copy instructions] (the last the default; on
phones the two copies move into the content), and the instructions carry
the code at a sentence end and the link on a line of its own. Without
both members S2 stays as in 1.8.2.

TV-W6 S11 to S13: one thread per process long-polls GET
/api/hjv/support-code/wait (rev, 30 s, 3-30 s backoff, a kick when the
app comes back) while a code of the login is open. A used code's PC ID
and key go into the support PCs table (memory only, tied to the login's
token, until the ticket ends). S2 shows the S11 line while it waits and
turns into S12 with [Connect]; once S2 was closed, S13 asks in the main
window. 401 ends the login as an account request's does; 403 or 404 is
a server without the waiting room and shows nothing.

TV-W6 controller proof (design 3-4, critic C-02, S-02): a PC outside
the account's list that is a support PC, over a secured channel under
the waiting room's key, gets 1.6.0's connection proof without any
password, once hjv-api answered the login within two minutes or answers
a waiting room request now. Another key sends no proof and no warning.
A support proof's refusal goes upstream's way (wait for Accept, or the
password box), not 1.6.0's "could not connect without a password".

TV-W6 S14, S15: the remote restart's confirm shows S14 alone for a
support PC of this login, and the offline text after that restart S15.

TV-W6 P4 to P6 (critic X-02, 2-5): the connection window draws kind
'staff' as the shield and 'Yonsei faculty or staff (verified login)' on
the mark line, P5 in the caution's place above [Accept] where the PC
shows that button, and P3's toast names the shield and the line.

New pure Dart test: test/hjviewer_support_test.dart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
